  "summary": {
    "derivative_id": "der:rc4:cb_df0f3eeee8874d31998efb3005f8676d:summary",
    "text": "AEIOU Foundation is an Australian charity that provided early intervention services for children aged 2\u20136 with an autism diagnosis. As shown on its website and in its 2023 regulatory filing, AEIOU describes itself as neurodiversity\u2011affirming and says it uses a combination of person\u2011first and identity\u2011first language based on feedback from a 2023 parent community study. The organisation lists a Brisbane office (Level 1, 15 Astor Terrace, Spring Hill, QLD), phone and email contact channels, weekday office hours, and secure online family payment functionality. AEIOU states it is developing a Reconciliation Action Plan. The organisation\u2019s website also includes a notice issued by the liquidators referring to \u201cAEIOU FOUNDATION (In Liquidation).\u201d"
  },
